ands of dollars in cash  to get this 30-minute outpatient  procedure you don't give a  addict cash money industry insiders told  us doctors made up to $30,000 in  insurance money for each simple surgery  and the money was so good  some doctors hired marketers and some of  those marketers hired recruiters who  lured vulnerable patients with cash as  part of our investigation we spoke  undercover with some of those marketers  and recruiters who pointed to a doctor  in Beverly Hills named Randy Rosen the  same doctor who did  Brennan buries implants excuse me dr.  Rosen two years ago Rosen declined our  request for an interview we've been  wanting to talk to you about why  patients are being paid to get surgeries  and said nothing to our producer outside  his office but now Rosen has been  charged with fraudulently billing  insurance companies over 650 million  dollars and stealing almost 52 million  dollars in what prosecutors say was an  elaborate scheme the district attorney  called Rosen a real-life Frankenstein  one of the many victims Brennan berry  who three months after getting his  procedure overdosed after taking heroin  mixed with fentanyl I came home found  I'm in his bedroom and he was cold and  when I got here after he died  Debbie berry learned her son was paid  $1,000 to get the knelt Rexona implant  she has been fighting to tell his story  ever since I'm doing this for my son I  think he would be proud that I'm doing  this I hope that he would be proud that  I'm doing this but I don't want he  didn't I don't want him to die in vain  we have a legitimate question sir what  if they get him convicted I've already  told the DA's office that I will fly to  California and I'll get on that stand  and I'll face that man look him right in  the eye and give a victim impact  statement I absolutely will do that you  think I'll get that chance I hope so I  hope so I want to face him I want to  face him and I want to tell him what  he's taking from me  and what I have to live with every day  for the rest of my life and what I'm  living without for the rest of my life  dr. Rosen pleaded not guilty to all  counts CBS News reached out to dr.  Rosen's attorney for comment multiple  times he has not responded to our  request we will continue to follow that  case as it develops
 

